#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""kbcparity — the cross-implementation evidence layer for kb-c.

kb-c is a C17 port of the Rust `kb` daemon. Every other gate in the port
compares kb-c against ITSELF: its own tests, its own benchmarks, its own
invariants. Nothing measured kb-c against the thing it is a port of, so
"matches the original" was a claim with nothing behind it. This harness is
the measurement: it drives the SAME pinned inputs through the Rust daemon
and through the C daemon and diffs what each one stored.

Two suites:

  capture  the stored artefact, byte for byte, and the front matter each
           daemon extracted from it, field by field
  links    the resolved edge set, the outcome of the resolution ladder for
           every wikilink, and the backlink count per document

WHY THE ALLOWLIST IS THE DESIGN, NOT A SUPPRESSION LIST. A harness that
reports correct behaviour as a failure within a week gets ignored, and this
port has already had that happen twice. So every KNOWN divergence lives in
divergences.v1.conf with a REASON (accepted trade-off, known parser
difference, unported original behaviour) and the date it was accepted, and
the run prints accepted divergences in a bucket of their own — never mixed
into the pass count. A divergence with no entry is a FAILURE.

The anti-absorption rule: an entry matches by (suite, field, subject-glob)
and an entry that matches NOTHING is reported STALE and fails the run, so
the list cannot quietly grow to cover everything and nobody can tell. The
entry count is compared against the previous run and the growth is printed.

WHY A BLOCKED RUN IS NOT A PASS. A harness that cannot tell "no divergence"
from "no comparison happened" is worse than no harness: it is a green light
wired to nothing. Every early exit that means the comparison did not happen
is SKIPPED-BLOCKED (exit 77) and says, in those words, which precondition
was missing. Exit 0 means the comparison RAN.

WHY A COMPARISON NOBODY MADE IS NOT A COMPARISON THAT AGREED. Every
declined comparison is a GAP or a STRUCTURAL gap, and they are counted,
named and printed separately. A GAP is one this run could have made and
did not — a precondition it did not meet — and it FAILS the run, with the
remedy that gap's own, so a run that already passed a flag is never told
to pass it again. A STRUCTURAL gap is a question no surface either daemon
implements can answer: it is printed every run with its count and its
reason, it does not fail the run, and it is never counted as a pass. The
line can therefore go green without anything having been hidden, and
FIELD COVERAGE prints how many documents each field was really compared on
so a pass count cannot be read as breadth it does not have.

WHAT THE FRONT MATTER IS READ FROM. The Rust document row
(GET /api/kb/{kb}/docs/{id}), not the list rows: /docs and /notes are
disjoint namespaces publishing different shapes, and the note row carries
no category, no created, no severity and no summary at all. Reading them
off the list row made a document that publishes all six front-matter
fields look like one that publishes none.

EXIT CODES
  0   every comparison either matched or matched an allowlist entry, and
      no comparison was left unmeasured for want of a precondition
  1   at least one unlisted divergence, a stale allowlist entry, or a GAP
      — a comparison this run could have made and did not
  3   HARD STOP: a pinned input does not match its SHA256SUMS
  77  SKIPPED-BLOCKED: the comparison could not be performed
  2   usage error
"""

